Renaissance thought: Thinkers like Marsilio Ficino and Giordano Bruno revived Hermetic texts, embedding "as above, so below" into European cosmology.

Modern esotericism: The phrase persists in occult traditions, Theosophy, and even contemporary metaphysics, symbolizing the unity of macrocosm and microcosm.

